  "html": "<div><section><div><section><p>This is the currently published alpha baseline and remains subject to final professional legal review.</p><div><blockquote><strong>INTERIM PUBLIC ALPHA BASELINE.</strong> This document governs the current experimental alpha and may be updated as the Service, law, and operational controls develop.</blockquote><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> August 17, 2026<br><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 20, 2026<br><strong>Document version:</strong> 0.4-public-alpha</p><p>This Notice explains how Tenvor Compute, which operates the Tenvor project from Richardson, Texas, United States, and its authentication/protection providers use cookies and browser storage on tenvor.io and related Tenvor domains. It supplements the <a href=\"/legal/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p><h2 id=\"1-current-position\">1. Current position</h2><p>As of the effective date, the reviewed Tenvor public-site bundle does not include a first-party analytics SDK, advertising SDK, behavioral-advertising pixel, or marketing cookie library. The site uses technologies necessary to provide authentication, protect sign-in, maintain a session, remember limited interface state, and recover an in-progress durable Playground job.</p><p>Tenvor does not currently use these technologies to sell personal data or serve cross-context behavioral advertising.</p><h2 id=\"2-necessary-authentication-cookies\">2. Necessary authentication cookies</h2><p>Tenvor uses Clerk for account authentication. Clerk sets cookies or similar identifiers needed to determine whether a user is signed in, maintain and refresh sessions, protect authentication flows, and prevent abuse. Depending on Clerk’s current implementation and Tenvor’s configuration, examples may include:</p><div><div class=\"s-tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Technology</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>__session</code> or equivalent session token</td><td>Clerk</td><td>Authenticate and refresh the signed-in session</td><td>Session or provider-configured lifetime</td></tr><tr><td><code>__client_uat</code> or equivalent state cookie</td><td>Clerk</td><td>Track authentication client update/sign-out state</td><td>Provider-configured lifetime</td></tr><tr><td>Clerk device, handshake, or development cookies</td><td>Clerk</td><td>Complete authentication, device, or domain handoff</td><td>Session or short-lived</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p>The exact names and durations may change when Clerk updates its service.</p><p>These cookies are necessary for managed sign-in. Blocking them may prevent account access, Playground use, API-key management, or other authenticated features.</p><h2 id=\"3-anti-bot-and-security-cookies\">3. Anti-bot and security cookies</h2><p>Clerk’s protection flow may use Cloudflare infrastructure, including a challenge or rate-protection cookie such as <code>_cfuvid</code>, to distinguish legitimate requests, reduce automated abuse, and protect authentication endpoints.</p><p>These technologies are used for security and are not intended for behavioral advertising. Blocking them may cause a challenge to repeat or sign-in to fail.</p><h2 id=\"4-tenvor-browser-storage\">4. Tenvor browser storage</h2><h3 id=\"playground-recovery\">Playground recovery</h3><p>The managed Playground may write a small, content-free recovery record to browser <code>sessionStorage</code>. It can include a Tenvor job or recovery identifier, the account identity to which it belongs, and bounded state needed to recover the same durable request after a reload.</p><p>The recovery record is designed not to contain:</p><ul><li>prompt or message content;</li><li>generated output;</li><li>a raw Tenvor API key;</li><li>a Clerk password;</li><li>private keys; or</li><li>the full inference request.</li></ul><p><code>sessionStorage</code> is normally scoped to the browser tab or session and is removed when the session ends or the record is cleared. Clearing the browser record does <strong>not</strong> cancel a running request or change ledger records.</p><h3 id=\"chat-work\">Chat &amp; Work</h3><p>Chat &amp; Work remembers your spend-cap choice and panel layout in browser <code>localStorage</code>, and the conversation you have open in <code>sessionStorage</code>. The spend-cap record is keyed by your Tenvor account ID. None of these records contains message or file content.</p><h3 id=\"interface-preferences\">Interface preferences</h3><p>The site or desktop node application may store limited local preferences such as theme, onboarding-completion, or presentation state. These preferences are local to the device and are not intended to identify you across unrelated services.</p><h2 id=\"5-no-marketing-cookie-controls-today\">5. No marketing-cookie controls today</h2><p>Because the current public site uses only necessary, security, authentication, and limited functional storage, it does not present a marketing-cookie consent panel. You can control cookies through your browser, but disabling necessary technologies may break authenticated functions.</p><p>Before adding analytics, advertising, session-replay, A/B testing, social-media pixels, or non-essential measurement, Tenvor must:</p><ol><li>update this Notice and the Privacy Policy;</li><li>determine whether opt-in consent or an opt-out mechanism is required by the user’s jurisdiction;</li><li>implement the appropriate preference controls before the technology loads; and</li><li>update the sale/sharing and Global Privacy Control disclosures.</li></ol><h2 id=\"6-how-to-inspect-or-clear-storage\">6. How to inspect or clear storage</h2><p>Most browsers let you view, block, or delete cookies and site storage through privacy or developer settings. Deleting authentication cookies signs you out. Deleting Playground recovery storage removes local recovery state but does not cancel an active server-side request or change ledger records.</p><p>Use the Service’s supported cancellation and privacy-request processes rather than relying on browser deletion for those actions.</p><h2 id=\"7-changes-and-contact\">7. Changes and contact</h2><p>We will update this Notice when our technologies or providers change.</p><p>Questions may be sent to <strong><a href=\"mailto:privacy@tenvor.io\">privacy@tenvor.io</a></strong>. Security concerns should be sent to <strong><a href=\"mailto:security@tenvor.io\">security@tenvor.io</a></strong>.</p></div></section></div></section></div>"
